"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-04T19:02:53Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T19:02:53Z","body":"Could you provide a MRP to test this issue?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2698620681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2699771371","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103543#issuecomment-2699771371","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103543","id":2699771371,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6g6z3r","user":{"login":"carsonetb","id":63245844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ1ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63245844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb","html_url":"https://github.com/carsonetb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-05T04:21:01Z","updated_at":"2025-03-05T04:21:01Z","body":"Sure thing.\n\nSee that it's working for now, go into Node3D script and uncomment the line setting rotation. \n\n[bugtest_2025-03-04_20-19-57.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19081839/bugtest_2025-03-04_20-19-57.zip)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2699771371/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706564268","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103543#issuecomment-2706564268","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103543","id":2706564268,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hUuSs","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T14:19:13Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T14:19:13Z","body":"There's a number of issues at play here.\n\n1. This isn't specific to Jolt Physics, and happens with Godot Physics as well.\n2. Setting any part of a `RigidBody3D` transform manually, either directly or through a parent, will cause all kinds of weird issues, as you'll be fighting against the physics simulation's own force integration. So this isn't related to `HingeJoint3D` per se. The same thing would happen if you were to set `position.y = 0` to try to \"cancel out\" a body's gravity.\n3. Even if it that wasn't the case, you should be doing this in `_physics_process`, not `_process`, since they run at different frequencies. This is why you're seeing random results.\n\nWhat exactly is it that you're hoping to achieve with rotating the body manually?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706564268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706707598","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103543#issuecomment-2706707598","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103543","id":2706707598,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVRSO","user":{"login":"carsonetb","id":63245844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ1ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63245844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb","html_url":"https://github.com/carsonetb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T15:14:52Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T15:14:52Z","body":"Well I guess what I'm expecting is to be able to move the HingeJoint, but not have the RigidBody affected by that movement. \nMaybe the problem is that I'm not using _physics_process.\nI'll check it out later, but thanks in advance!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706707598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706743945","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103543#issuecomment-2706743945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103543","id":2706743945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hVaKJ","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-07T15:30:29Z","updated_at":"2025-03-07T15:35:40Z","body":"> Well I guess what I'm expecting is to be able to move the HingeJoint, but not have the RigidBody affected by that movement.\n\nMoving a joint node isn't technically something you can do in the first place, as the joint node's transform is basically just used to express the initial conditions of the constraint between the two bodies. You can think of a joint's transform as being irrelevant once `_ready` has been called on it.\n\nWhat you likely want instead is to create a second body to serve as the \"anchor\" body, attach that to `node_a` of the joint and then have your `RigidBody3D` be `node_b` instead. That way you can move the anchor body around and (in a manner of speaking) the effective hinge joint along with it.\n\nNote that this anchor must be a _kinematic_ body if you're planning to move it around, meaning either an `AnimatableBody3D`, a `RigidBody3D` with `freeze` enabled and `freeze_mode` set to \"Kinematic\", or a `CharacterBody3D`. You should not use a `StaticBody3D`.\n\nAlso note that this means you'll need `top_level` set on your `RigidBody3D` if you absolutely must have it childed to something that's going to be moving.\n\nHere's a modified version of your MRP that hopefully illustrates all this: [hinge-anchor.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19129076/hinge-anchor.zip)\n\nEDIT: I forgot to clear the `collision_layer` and `collision_mask` of the anchor body in the MRP, which you'd likely want to do, if you don't want it to collide with anything else.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2706743945/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709019757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103543#issuecomment-2709019757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103543","id":2709019757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6heFxt","user":{"login":"carsonetb","id":63245844,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMjQ1ODQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63245844?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb","html_url":"https://github.com/carsonetb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carsonetb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-09T19:02:29Z","updated_at":"2025-03-09T19:02:29Z","body":"Sorry for the late response ...\n\nThanks for all this information!\n\nI do think that if this is intended to happen then the physics engine should break in a much more obvious way. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2709019757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]